# Allowlist, not a denylist (review finding): the Dockerfile only ever
# COPYs pyproject.toml/uv.lock/.python-version/src/ (deploy/compose/
# docker-compose.yml's `embedding-sidecar` service builds this whole
# directory as its context), so `*` excludes everything by default and only
# those paths are let back in below. A denylist that names just the known
# junk (.venv/, caches) instead still hands the build context - and
# therefore the image's build history - any `.env*` file, private key, or
# other real local data a developer happens to have sitting under this
# directory, none of which the image needs.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!src
!src/**
